From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: GloriousEggroll <gloriouseggroll@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 19 Aug 2026 00:00:00 -0600
Subject: [PATCH] ntdll: Reuse the effective range after clearing native views

The native-view recovery path was originally written when alloc_free_area()
accepted one already-resolved address limit.  Its rebase onto Wine's newer
low/high-limit API passed the raw optional limits to the second attempt
instead.  Ordinary NtAllocateVirtualMemory() calls use zero for both optional
limits, leaving the retry with an empty range.  It also lost the host-page
rounding applied to the first attempt.

Retry with the effective start/end range and rounded host size calculated by
map_view().  This allows 32-bit applications to recover after native mappings
are removed instead of returning STATUS_NO_MEMORY for every probe.  FreeArc
installers otherwise recurse while probing available memory and eventually
overflow the decompression worker's stack.
---
 dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
index df31b195d0e..57feae114b0 100644
--- a/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
+++ b/dlls/ntdll/unix/virtual.c
@@ -2560,7 +2560,7 @@ static NTSTATUS map_view( struct file_view **view_ret, void *base, size_t size,
 
             clear_native_views();
             if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = FALSE;
-            ptr = alloc_free_area( (void *)limit_low, (void *)limit_high, size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask );
+            ptr = alloc_free_area( start, end, host_size, top_down, unix_prot, align_mask );
             if (!is_win64) increase_try_map_step = TRUE;
             if (!ptr) return STATUS_NO_MEMORY;
         }
